      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q5-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The probability of winning one game is 3 ! 15 (1/6)k(5/6)15−k ≈0.23152 . p = 1 − X [M1] [A1] k k=0  = 252, with five wins and (d) The number of wins in ten independent games is B(10, p). [B1] Here 10 5 five losses: Use p from part (c) to get ! 10 p5(1 −p)5 ≈0.04493 . [M1] [A1] 5\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
