    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-e/q6",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q6-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A bag contains blue, yellow and red discs and these discs show on their face a single digit whole number. The probability of drawing a blue disc is 1 2 , the probability of drawing a yellow disc is 1 3 and the probability of drawing a red disc is 1 6 . 12 of the blue discs show an even number, 5 5 8 of the yellow discs show an even number and 1 4 of the red discs show an even number. A disc is drawn at random from the bag. ( ) 4 a) Determine the probability that the disc will show an even number.\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q6-question-2.svg\" alt=\"b) Given that the disc that was drawn was showing an even number, find the probability that the disc was not red. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:582.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q6-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Using a tree diagram for this problem:\" style=\"--madas-width:505.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q6-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Let E be the event that the disc shows an even number: The even branches are P(blue ∩E) = 1 12 = 5 5 P(yellow ∩E) = 1 5 8 = 5 P(red ∩E) = 1 1 4 = 1 24, 24, 24. 2 3 6 (a) Adding gives P(E) = 11/24 .\" style=\"--madas-width:590.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q6-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"[A1] Blue and even [A1] yellow and even [A1] red and even [A1] sum the joint probabilities (b) The numerator for “not red and even is P(B ∩E) + P(Y ∩E) = 5/24 + 5/24. The tree and Venn representations give the same disjoint events: Divide by P(E) = 11/24. The conditional probability is (5/24 + 5/24)/(11/24) = 10/11 . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 6 is 7 marks.</p>"
