    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A light rigid rod AB , where A is vertically above B , has a particle of mass  0.2 kg attached to it at A and a particle of mass 0.3 kg attached to it at B . The loaded rod is accelerated vertically upwards by a vertical force of magnitude 6 N , applied to B . Find the thrust in the rod. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a diagram - mark the thrusts as tensions:\" style=\"--madas-width:429.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q10-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Let T be the thrust and take upwards as positive: [M1] The source first assumes tension S: on A, −S −0.2g = 0.2a; on B, 6 + S −0.3g = 0.3a. Adding eliminates S. Using the complete system, a = 2.2 m s−2. 6 −0.5g = 0.5a =⇒ [M1] [A1] The first equation gives S = −0.2(g + a) = −0.2(12) = −2.4, so the connecting rod is in compression and its thrust is positive: For particle A, T −0.2g = 0.2a. [A1] Thus T = 0.2(9.8 + 2.2) = 2.4 N . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 10 is 6 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A light rigid rod AB , where A is vertically above B , has a particle of mass  0.2 kg attached to it at A and a particle of mass 0.3 kg attached to it at B . The loaded rod is accelerated vertically upwards by a vertical force of magnitude 6 N , applied to B . Find the thrust in the rod. ( ) 6"
