    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q11-question-1.svg\" alt=\"50 N 100 N 40° 20kg 20° The figure above shows a small box of mass 20 kg , pulled by two light inextensible strings along rough horizontal ground. The tension in the rope inclined at 20° to the horizontal is 100 N .\" style=\"--madas-width:560.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q11-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The tension in the rope inclined at 40° to the horizontal is 50 N . The box is modelled as a particle in equilibrium, experiencing a constant frictional force of F N and a normal reaction of R N . Determine the value of R and the value of F . ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q11-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Starting with a diagram: The upward components of both tensions reduce the normal reaction: [M1] The rightward horizontal component of the larger tension exceeds the leftward component of the smaller tension, so friction acts to the left: [A1] Equilibrium gives R + 100 sin 20◦+ 50 sin 40◦= 20g,\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q11-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"F + 50 cos 40◦= 100 cos 20◦. [A1] Rearrange separately: R = 196 −100 sin 20◦−50 sin 40◦, and F = 100 cos 20◦−50 cos 40◦. Thus R ≈129.66 [A1] and F ≈55.67 , [A1] measured in newtons: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 11 is 6 marks.</p>"
    ],
