    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-e/q12",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A non uniform ladder of weight 180 N and length 6 metres, rests with its end A on smooth horizontal ground and its end B against a rough vertical wall. The coefficient of friction between the ladder and the wall is 1 4 . The centre of mass of the ladder is 1.5 metres from A . The ladder lies in a vertical plane perpendicular to the wall and the ground, and is inclined at an angle θ to the horizontal, where tan θ = 2 . A man can just prevent the ladder from sliding down the wall by pushing the bottom of the ladder with a horizontal force F . ( ) 6 By modelling the ladder as a non uniform rod determine the value of F .\" style=\"--madas-width:570.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q12-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q12-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Worked solution diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:445.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q12-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Let N be the horizontal wall reaction and R the vertical ground reaction: [M1] The limiting friction at the wall acts upwards and has magnitude N/4. [A1] Vertical equilibrium gives R + N/4 = 180. Since the ground is smooth, horizontal equilibrium gives F = N. Taking moments about A Taking moments about A gives 180(1.5 cos θ) = N(6 sin θ) + N 4 (6 cos θ). [M1] Divide by 6 cos θ. [A1] The handwritten form before dividing by six is 270 = 6F tan θ + 6F/4 . = 12F + 3F/2 Double both sides to give 540 = 27F. Equivalently, 45 = N(tan θ + 1 4) , [A1] = 9 4N\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q12-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"so F = 20 N . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 12 is 6 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A non uniform ladder of weight 180 N and length 6 metres, rests with its end A on smooth horizontal ground and its end B against a rough vertical wall. The coefficient of friction between the ladder and the wall is 1 4 . The centre of mass of the ladder is 1.5 metres from A . The ladder lies in a vertical plane perpendicular to the wall and the ground, and is inclined at an angle θ to the horizontal, where tan θ = 2 . A man can just prevent the ladder from sliding down the wall by pushing the bottom of the ladder with a horizontal force F . ( ) 6 By modelling the ladder as a non uniform rod determine the value of F . "
