      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q14-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Differentiate velocity: a = 2t −4. [M1] At t = 3, a = 2 m s−2 . [M1] [A1] (b) At rest, 0 = t2 −4t −12 = (t −6)(t + 2). [M1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q14-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The two candidate times are 6, −2; discard the negative time: For t ≥0 this gives t = 6 [A1] and a = 8 m s−2 . [M1] [A1] (c) Integrating v and using x(0) = 20 [M1] gives x = t3/3 −2t2 −12t + 20. [A1] Equivalently, the signed area under the velocity graph is [t3/3 −2t2 −12t]6 0 = 72 −72 −72 . = −72 Add the initial position 20 to obtain −52. At t = 6, x = −52, [A1] so the distance from O is 52 m . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
