    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q15-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A 22m B 40° A particle P slides with constant acceleration down the line of greatest slope of a rough plane inclined at 40° to the horizontal. The particle covers a distance AB , where AB = 22 m , in 4 s .\" style=\"--madas-width:529.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q15-question-2.svg\" alt=\"ms−, calculate … 1 a) Given the speed of P at A is 3 i. … the speed of  P at B . ( ) 2 ii. … the acceleration of P . ( ) 2 b) Hence find the coefficient of friction between the particle and the plane. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:585.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q15-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Looking at the diagram below: (a) The source first uses s = ut + 1 2at2: 22 = 3(4) + 1 2a(42) = 12 + 8a; hence 8a = 10, a = 1.25. Then v = u + at = 3 + 1.25(4) .\" style=\"--madas-width:618.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q15-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"= 8 The same quantities can be found in the order requested: Take the direction down the slope as positive: (i) 22 = (3 + v)(4)/2, [B1] so v = 8 m s−1 . [A1] (ii) 8 = 3 + 4a, [B1] so a = 1.25 m s−2 . [A1] (b) For particle mass m, the normal reaction is mg cos 40◦. [B1] [A1] The equation down the slope is mg sin 40◦−µmg cos 40◦= m(1.25). [M1] [A1] Cancel the positive mass: g sin 40◦−µg cos 40◦= 1.25. Move the friction term to the other side before dividing: Therefore µ = g sin 40◦−1.25 ≈0.673 . [M1] [A1] g cos 40◦\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 15 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
