    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-e/q16",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q16-question-1.svg\" alt=\"D C A B 5 m 2 m 1 m A uniform rod AB has length 5 m and weight 300 N . The rod rests in a horizontal position on two smooth supports at C and D , where AC = 1 m and DB = 2 m , as shown in the figure above.\" style=\"--madas-width:560.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q16-question-2.svg\" alt=\"A particle of weight W N is placed on the rod at the point E , where AE x = m . The magnitude of the reaction on the rod at C is twice the magnitude of the reaction on the rod at D . a) Show clearly that 750 W = . ( ) 7 5 − 3 x b) Determine the range of possible values of x . ( ) 1\" style=\"--madas-width:572.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q16-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Start with a diagram: Let R be the reaction at D, so the reaction at C is 2R. (a) Taking moments about A Vertical balance gives 3R = 300 + W. [M1] [A1] Moments about A give 2R(1) + R(3) = 300(2.5) + Wx. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q16-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Substituting for R, 5(300 + W) = 750 + Wx =⇒ W(5 −3x) = 750. [M1] [A1] 3 Multiply the moment equation by 3 to obtain 1500 + 5W = 2250 + 3Wx, 5W −3Wx = 750. Hence W = 750/(5 −3x) . [M1] [A1] (b) A positive W requires 5 −3x &gt; 0. Taking E as distinct from A, as in the handwritten solution, the possible range is 0 &lt; x &lt; 5/3 . If placement at A is allowed, x = 0 also satisfies the equilibrium conditions: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 16 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
