    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-e/q17",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q17-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A particle A is released from rest from a point h m above level horizontal ground. One second later, another particle B is projected vertically downwards with speed ms− from the same point, A was released. 1 19.6 Given that the particles reach the ground at the same time, determine the value of h . ( ) 8\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q17-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Start with a detailed diagram: Take downwards as positive and let t be the flight time of B. [M1] The flight time of A is t + 1. [A1] Both cover the same distance: h = 4.9(t + 1)2 [M1] [A1] = 19.6t + 4.9t2.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q17-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Cancelling 4.9t2 gives 9.8t + 4.9 = 19.6t, [A1] so t = 0.5 s. [A1] Equivalently the source uses T = t + 1, timing from the release of A. Then 4.9T 2 = 19.6(T −1) + 4.9(T −1)2, so T 2 = 4T −4 + T 2 −2T + 1, giving 2T = 3, T = 1.5. Therefore h = 4.9(1.5)2 = 11.025 m . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 17 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A particle A is released from rest from a point h m above level horizontal ground. One second later, another particle B is projected vertically downwards with speed ms− from the same point, A was released. 1 19.6 Given that the particles reach the ground at the same time, determine the value of h . ( ) 8"
  },
