    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-e/q18",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q18-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Relative to a fixed origin O , the horizontal unit vectors i and j are pointing due east and due north, respectively. At time t = 0 s a footballer A kicks the ball from the point with position vector ms− in the direction ( 1 ( 4 i + 2 j m giving it a constant speed of 10 ) 4 i + 3 j . ) The ball is modelled as a particle moving with constant velocity. a) Show that the position vector of the ball, t s after it was kicked, is given by ( ) ( 8 t + 4 ) i + ( 6 t + 2 ) j. 4 You may not use the answer to verify this part.\" style=\"--madas-width:574.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q18-question-2.svg\" alt=\"At time t = 0 s , another footballer B is observed to be running through the point with position vector ( 11 i + 23 j m . ) ms−. 1 Footballer B is modelled as a particle running due East with constant speed U b) Given that B intercepts the ball determine the value of U . ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q18-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Looking at a diagram - note B is running fast: (a) The direction 4i + 3j has magnitude 5. [B1] Multiplying its unit vector by the speed 10 gives v = 8i + 6j. [A1] Add tv to the ball’s starting position: r = (4i + 2j) + t(8i + 6j) [M1] [A1] = (8t + 4)i + (6t + 2)j .\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-e/q18-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) The position of B is (11 + Ut)i + 23j. [B1] Equality of the north components gives 6t + 2 = 23, so t = 3.5. [A1] The east components then give 11 + 3.5U = 8(3.5) + 4 , [A1] = 32 so the eastward displacement is 32 −11 = 21 metres in 3.5 seconds: Dividing gives U = 6 m s−1 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 18 is 8 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "Relative to a fixed origin O , the horizontal unit vectors i and j are pointing due east and due north, respectively. At time t = 0 s a footballer A kicks the ball from the point with position vector ms− in the direction ( 1 ( 4 i + 2 j m giving it a constant speed of 10 ) 4 i + 3 j . ) The ball is modelled as a particle moving with constant velocity. a) Show that the position vector of the ball, t s after it was kicked, is given by ( ) ( 8 t + 4 ) i + ( 6 t + 2 ) j. 4 You may not use the answer to verify this part. At time t = 0 s , another footballer B is observed to be running through the point with position vector ( 11 i + 23 j m . ) ms−. 1 Footballer B is modelled as a particle running due East with constant speed U b) Given that B intercepts the ball determine the value of U . ( ) 4"
